CxD Global Deployment & Regional Isolation Guide

This guide ensures that developers can launch the CxD Governance Engine for their specific nation without risk of crosstalk, data leaks, or regional confusion.

1. Regional Namespacing (The "No-Crosstalk" Rule)

To prevent Madagascar data from mixing with Sri Lanka data, every deployment must define a unique REGION_ID.

Action: Update App.jsx

Locate the CONFIGURATION block and set the ISO-3166-1 alpha-3 code:

Sri Lanka: LKA

Madagascar: MDG

Hispaniola: HSP

Why this works:

The REGION_ID is appended to the hardware UUID before hashing. This means a user's "Vote ID" in Madagascar is mathematically different from their "Vote ID" in Sri Lanka, even if they use the same phone.

2. Infrastructure Isolation

Never point multiple apps to the same consensus cluster.

Unique API Endpoints: Every developer must deploy their own C-Node cluster. In App.jsx, the API_URL must point to the specific Azure Container Instance created by your deployment script.

Azure Tagging: Our deployment scripts (ops/deploy.sh) automatically tag resources with country=CODE. Use these tags to monitor costs and traffic per region independently.

3. The "Secret Pepper"

The CXD_PEPPER environment variable in the C server is the ultimate firewall.

Rule: Every nation MUST use a different 64-character random string for their pepper.

If two countries use the same pepper, a hardware ID might produce the same hash. If they are different, crosstalk is mathematically impossible.

4. Step-by-Step Launch Sequence

Redraw the Land: Run python tools/nation_builder.py and type your country name. This updates the local map and geofence.

Set the Dialect: Update ENABLED_LANGUAGES and DICTIONARY in App.jsx.

Configure the Ballot: Update the PROPOSALS array with local issues.

Deploy the Hub: Run ./ops/deploy_national_emergency.sh. Note the generated URL.

Connect the App: Paste that URL into the App.jsx fetch logic.

Distribute: Host the React App as a PWA (Progressive Web App).

5. Avoiding Confusion in GitHub

If you are managing multiple countries:

Create separate branches (e.g., branch: madagascar, branch: sri-lanka).

The CONSTITUTION.md should be updated per branch to reflect local juror requirements.
